# Where tests/acceptance.sh finds the planted kit. Copy this file to tests/paths.local.env (git ignores it)
# and fill in your own path. An environment variable of the same name overrides the file. quill itself needs
# none of this: it builds and passes --selftest without the kit.
#
# The planted kit is the Python prototype quill was checked against; it is not part of this repository.
# Its folder articles/ holds the recurrent article folders that check-kit reads (README section 4.5):
# R0_memoryless, R1_plain, R1_rewired, R2_quotient, R3_overcomplete, R4_two_bits, R5_redundant,
# R9_session and C1_even.

# The kit's folder, the one that holds articles/.
QUILL_KIT=/path/to/kit

# Optional: the executable to test. The default is quill.exe at the root of this repository.
# QUILL_EXE=/path/to/quill.exe
